    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a spiced, bean-loaded dinner with sour cream on top. Cans and rice are doing the work here, and cans and rice are cheap.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCanned beans and canned corn are the whole base.\u003c/strong\u003e Watch the case price, buy deep when it drops, and you have the bones of this soup on the shelf for a year.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eMake your own taco seasoning from pantry jars.\u003c/strong\u003e The little packets cost more per ounce than almost anything else in the store, and it is chili powder, cumin, onion powder and salt you already own.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eTomato sauce, not salsa or diced tomatoes.\u003c/strong\u003e Plain tomato sauce is the cheapest tomato in the aisle and it gives this soup the smooth body it needs.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eLight sour cream is a topping, not an ingredient.\u003c/strong\u003e Add it to each container at reheat time instead of stirring it into the pot, and it will not break or go watery in the fridge."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Cook the rice separately per the package and set it aside covered.",
                    "Brown the ground turkey in the vegetable oil in your big pot over medium-high heat, breaking it up until it is cooked through.",
                    "Stir in the taco seasoning, onion powder, salt and black pepper and let them toast against the hot pan for a minute.",
                    "Pour in the tomato sauce and the chicken broth and bring it to a simmer.",
                    "Add the drained kidney beans and the drained sweet corn along with the touch of sugar-free maple syrup, which balances the acid in the tomato.",
                    "Simmer 20 minutes so the flavors settle, then taste and adjust the salt. Keep the sour cream on the side."
                ],
